# Test: fib-vpp programs an MPLS label push for a BGP labeled unicast route.
#
# Flow: the native driver starts three processes in order:
#   1. vpp_stub on a per-test Unix socket, JSONL log.
#   2. ze-peer on a dynamic port with a send-route directive that sends
#      a BGP UPDATE with labeled unicast NLRI (ipv4/mpls-label, SAFI 4)
#      for 10.30.0.0/24 label 100 next-hop 10.0.0.1.
#   3. ze with vpp.external=true and fib.vpp.enabled=true, with
#      ipv4/mpls-label family negotiated. Ze dials 127.0.0.1:$PORT,
#      receives the labeled UPDATE, nlrisplit strips the label,
#      RIB stores the route + label side-data, best-change propagates
#      labels through sysRIB, fib-vpp builds an ip_route_add_del with
#      LabelStack, stub logs it.
# The driver polls the stub's JSONL log for ip_route_add_del is_add=true
# prefix=10.30.0.0/24 with labels=[100], reports OK, then shuts down.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-vpp-3-mpls AC-1 -- labeled unicast -> VPP MPLS label push
# PREVENTS:  full-chain gap (labeled NLRI never entering RIB, labels not
#            flowing through best-change/sysRIB, fib-vpp not dispatching
#            to MPLS backend).

tmpfs=peer-script:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=20s
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.30.0.0/24:next-hop=10.0.0.1:origin-as=65001:label=100
EOF_PEER


cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture vpp/vpp-mpls-push $PORT:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: fib-vpp programmed 10.30.0.0/24 with label 100 into stub
